    "title": "Substring With Concatenation of All Words",
    "category": "Sliding Window",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "problemStatement": "You are given a string S and an array of words, where every word has the same length. Find all starting indices of substrings in S that are formed by concatenating every word exactly once and without any intervening characters. The words may appear in any order.",
    "input": "\u2022 First line contains string S. \u2022 Second line contains integer M. \u2022 Third line contains M space-separated words.",
    "output": "\u2022 Print all valid starting indices in increasing order. If none exist, print -1.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 1 \u2264 |S| \u2264 2 \u00d7 10^5 \u2022 1 \u2264 M \u2264 5000 \u2022 All words have equal length."
